---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import AffiliateLink from "../../components/AffiliateLink.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Red Dead Redemption 2 — Cross-Platform Buying Guide"
  description="Red Dead Redemption 2 buying guide: the masterpiece western, editions, and where to buy the digital version cheapest."
>
  <article class="post">
    <h1>Red Dead Redemption 2 — Cross-Platform Buying Guide</h1>
    <p class="meta">Xbox / PS5 / PC · Updated 2026-08-05</p>

    <p>
      <strong>Red Dead Redemption 2</strong> is Rockstar's 2018 western masterpiece — a
      story-driven open world widely considered one of the greatest games ever made. Six
      years on, it's also one of the cheapest premium games you can buy.
    </p>

    <h2>What you get</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Story mode</strong> — a 60+ hour single-player epic</li>
      <li><strong>Red Dead Online</strong> — a separate multiplayer mode, included but lightly supported now</li>
      <li><strong>Ultimate Edition</strong> — adds cash bonuses and survival kits; not worth it for story players</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where to buy cheapest</h2>
    <p>
      RDR2 sits at its lowest-ever key price. Green Man Gaming routinely beats both the
      console stores and physical discs, and a digital key means no disc to swap. On PC,
      compare against Steam sales too.
    </p>

    <ul class="buy-list">
      <li>
        <AffiliateLink
          network="gmg"
          href="https://www.greenmangaming.com/search/?q=red+dead+redemption+2"
          cta="Check Green Man Gaming"
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <AffiliateLink
          network="amazon"
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Red+Dead+Redemption+2"
          cta="Check on Amazon"
        />
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="note">
      Prices change frequently — always verify on the store before purchasing.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .post { padding: 1.5rem 0; max-width: 720px; }
  .post h1 { font-size: 1.8rem; }
  .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .buy-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; }
  .note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
</style>
